      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T23:33:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It won\u0027t be allowed to be promoted to X. However, X is still determined by these \"minimum node priority\" settings. If we change the settings then X can become a different value (lower), and the kernel could allow a downgrade.\n\nI don\u0027t think we want to lower the \"minimum node priority\" just because a process can\u0027t inherit realtime.",
      "parentUuid": "55c54b7b_1dce2412",
      "revId": "6600ba5dca3990e48f2322fdda09058455509989",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
